    rdfs:label "'] \\& |[schemanode]| $VetCarePlan77$ tikzcd% Universal property of the Mittens cocone: the type leg and domestic-class leg both factor through \\(\\) before reaching \\(VetCarePlan77\\) via the unique mediator \\(u\\). Any object that would replace \\(\\) must produce a second incompatible apex.fig:music-mittens-universal-property theorem[Mittens cocone uniqueness] thm:music-mittens-cocone-uniqueness Let the Music source diagram \\(D:J\\) have a compatible cocone with apex \\(\\). For any other compatible cocone target \\(VetCarePlan77\\) (a clinical summary that receives the same Mittens type and domestic-class observations along compatible arrows), there exists a unique mediating morphism \\[ u:77 \\] such that \\(toVetPlanj = uj\\) for all legs \\(j J\\). theorem proof Step 1 (legs). The type leg \\(type\\) and domestic-class leg \\(dc\\) are cocone maps from the source objects to \\(\\). Step 2 (compatibility). For \\(VetCarePlan77\\) to receive both observations, the arrows \\(toVetPlantype\\) and \\(toVetPlandc\\) must satisfy the compatibility condition on the governing arrow \\(subclassOf:domesticClass\\). Step 3 (base topic). The universal property of colimits licenses the unique mediator. Step 4 (anchor). The vet-care plan cannot be a second ``Mittens'' because the existing cocone already provides the unique path; any duplicate apex introduces an arrow that does not commute with \\(type\\). Step 5 (Yoneda). By Yoneda, any natural transformation \\((-,)(-,VetCarePlan77)\\) corresponds exactly to the unique \\(u\\). Step 6 (recap). \\(\\) is the initial compatible apex; the mediator \\(u\\) is unique. proof Diagram law (Figure~fig:music-mittens-universal-property): the two paths to \\(VetCarePlan77\\) commute through \\(\\), so the Music engine may not mint a second cat identity when the source legs already glue. [0.90]% tikzcd[column sep=large,row sep=large,ampersand replacement=\\&] |[classnode]| TaxonomyWitness [r," .
